{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task is AGENT-TF-01, implementing a Toolformer-style API call filtering mechanism.\n\nFrom the candidate artifact description:\n1. For each call, compute: `gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n2. Normalize gain by prediction tokens: `normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens`\n3. Accept a call if: `parseable == True` AND `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n4. Return `accepted_call_ids` (list of strings) and `diagnostics` (list of objects with `call_id`, `accepted`, `normalized_gain`)\n5. Keep diagnostics in supplied call order\n6. Round per-call diagnostics (normalized_gain should be rounded)\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture:\n- threshold = 0.05\n- call0: gain = 1.94835097 - 0.38569502 = 1.56265595, norm_gain = 1.56265595 / 5 = 0.3125319, parseable=True → accepted\n- call1: gain = 1.06116273 - 0.68319969 = 0.37796304, norm_gain = 0.37796304 / 4 = 0.09449076, parseable=True → accepted\n- call2: gain = 1.21810502 - 0.47260371 = 0.74550131, norm_gain = 0.74550131 / 6 = 0.12425022, parseable=True → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.05721833 - 0.29767903 = 0.7595393, norm_gain = 0.7595393 / 5 = 0.15190786, parseable=True → accepted\n- call4: gain = 1.06717367 - 0.85733566 = 0.20983801, norm_gain = 0.20983801 / 5 = 0.04196760, parseable=True → 0.04196760 \u003c 0.05 → rejected\n- call5: gain = 1.66191711 - 0.89798497 = 0.76393214, norm_gain = 0.76393214 / 4 = 0.190983035, parseable=True → accepted\n\nSo accepted: call0, call1, call2, call3, call5 (not call4)\n\nThe description mentions \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - I need to figure out the rounding. Let me think about this. The description says \"rounded\" but doesn't specify precision. Looking at the schema, `normalized_gain` is just a `number`. I'll round to some reasonable precision - maybe the artifact means rounding to a standard number of decimal places. Let me think...\n\nThe description says \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" This likely means rounding normalized_gain to some number of decimal places. Given the input values have 8 decimal places, maybe round to 4 or 5 decimal places? Or maybe it just means round to float (no specific rounding beyond floating point)?\n\nActually, looking more carefully - the description might just mean that values are normal floats (not requiring infinite precision). I'll keep them as Python floats without special rounding, or perhaps round to a reasonable number of decimal places like 4.\n\nWait, let me re-read: \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" - This suggests rounding is significant. Maybe round to 4 decimal places? Or maybe it's specific to the task.\n\nI'll implement it with rounding to 4 decimal places since the normalized gains look like they have 4-5 significant figures.\n\nActually, I think the simplest approach is to just return the float as-is (Python floating point). The \"rounded\" might just be a general description meaning \"computed to a sensible precision.\" I'll go with returning the actual computed float value.\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"threshold must be a number\")\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls must be a list\")\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be at least 1 for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\n        \n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"accepted\": accepted,\n            \"normalized_gain\": round(normalized_gain, 4)\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nWait, the instruction says to round diagnostics. I'll round to 4 decimal places.\n\nLet me check case 002 - call4 has `parseable: false`:\n- gain = 1.35899862 - 0.11897463 = 1.24002399\n- normalized_gain = 1.24002399 / 4 = 0.310005998\n- parseable = False → rejected (even though normalized_gain \u003e threshold)\n\nThis seems correct.\n\nNow let me format the output properly. The response must be a single JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source code as a string.\n\nLet me write the final implementation carefully:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"threshold must be a number\")\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls must be a list\")\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if not isinstance(prediction_tokens, int) or prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be a positive integer for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\n        \n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"accepted\": accepted,\n            \"normalized_gain\": round(normalized_gain, 4)\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nNow I need to encode this as a JSON string with proper escaping of newlines and special characters, and wrap it in `{\"implementation\": \"...\"}`.\n\nThe response must be exactly one JSON object with key \"implementation\". No markdown, no fences, no extra text.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"threshold must be a number\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        if not isinstance(prediction_tokens, int) or prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\\n            raise ValueError(\\n                f\\\"prediction_tokens must be a positive integer for call {call_id}\\\"\\n            )\\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"loss_without_call must be a number for call {call_id}\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"loss_with_call must be a number for call {call_id}\\\")\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\\n\\n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": round(normalized_gain, 4)\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01BXcde9detORTgtt9fnof7p","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2484,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":35,"output_tokens":2171,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1729},"service_tier":"standard"}}